# StageVerify lean agent process (PR #257 process)

SSOT for review lanes, merge/deploy, and always-loaded rules. **Supersedes D-60 and D-65.** Amends D-92 / D-93 (Composer still codes first; extra model passes run only when this file says so). Older `.cursor/rules/*` files are on-demand — if they conflict with this file, **this file wins**.

## Session start

1. Read **this file** and `PROJECT_STATUS/STATE_SUMMARY.md` only (lean startup).
2. Before any work: `git fetch origin main && git pull origin main`, then confirm PR #257 tip `a69dc81c` is an ancestor of HEAD: `git merge-base --is-ancestor a69dc81c HEAD`.
3. Run `npm run gate:tier` (or `node scripts/gate-check.mjs --classify --files …`) on **planned paths** before coding — **path rules decide tier; Composer self-label never does.**
4. Open `CURRENT_STATE.md`, `MEMORY.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, or `MODEL_DOSSIER.md` only when the task needs them.
5. **256k context cap:** no Cursor agent may exceed a **256k** context window (cost beyond that). Use the **standard** context setting. For Grok 4.7: **context=256k, never 500k or max**. Read only the files the job needs. If a job looks like it will approach 256k, **stop** and **hand off to a fresh agent with a short summary** — do not continue.

## One job

One small job / one small PR per agent. Read only the files you need. PR body must include the **MODEL EVIDENCE** block (exact fields below) plus what changed, why, how to test, rollback, `ladder-step:`. No reviewer swarms.

### MODEL EVIDENCE (every PR)

- `job-type:` one of `firestore-rules/auth` | `money/billing` | `cloud-functions-logic` | `ui-change` | `tests-only` | `ci/gate` | `docs/process`
- `risk-tier:` `HIGH` | `MEDIUM` | `LOW` (from `gate:tier`, not Composer)
- `builder-model:` and `ladder-step:`
- `reviewer-models:` exact allowlisted gate slugs used (e.g. `grok-4.7-high` — Grok 4.7, reasoning_effort HIGH, fast OFF, context 256k) so MODEL EVIDENCE distinguishes Grok versions
- `model:` in review evidence is the **gate slug only** (example `grok-4.7-high`). The reviewer's self-reported model is a separate line `model-self-report:`. `model-self-report:` does **not** satisfy `model:`. CI does not require `model-self-report:`.
- `context-used:` peak token total Cursor shows for that reviewer run. Read it in the **Agents** window: click the **context ring** next to the prompt input; the tray lists token totals (system prompt, tools, rules, skills, MCP, subagents, summarized conversation, conversation). Record the **highest overall total** shown during the review. Use `n/a` only when that ring, or another Cursor usage readout for the same run, shows no number — do not guess. This cloud run-info API does not return token counts. CI does not check the value.
- `sonnet-ran:` `required` | `no` only. Never `optional`.
- `sonnet-unique-findings:` `Y` or `N` plus brief what
- `confidence:` builder’s numeric confidence at handoff (integer percent, e.g. `97` — no rounding up)

**Builder confidence (97% rule, Dan 2026-10-15; D-95):** Complements D-69 / `.cursor/rules/confidence-gate.mdc` (pre-edit ≥97% before repo writes; terminal **DONE** only when handoff confidence ≥97%). Every builder also states handoff `confidence:` in MODEL EVIDENCE. **Target ≥97%** before handoff. If under 97%, do **not** hand off as fully done: step up the coding ladder (§ Coding ladder) or tighten checks (re-run targeted tests, narrow scope, fix gaps), then re-state `confidence:`; if still under 97%, say so plainly in the PR body and the completion report (terminal **PARTIAL** or **BLOCKED** per `done-signal.mdc` — not **DONE**). **Merge (Spot):** Spot **may** merge without asking Dan only when **all** hold: MODEL EVIDENCE `confidence:` **≥97**; Grok **accuracy** review recorded **PASS** (no FAIL/HIGH findings; missing or NOT RUN → ask Dan); PR CI green; HIGH mechanical evidence (`security-gate-id:`, `model:`, `reviewed-commit:` when HIGH) already satisfied; and `sonnet-ran:` is **no** (when `sonnet-ran:` is **required**, or any Sonnet-backup path per `requiresSonnetBackup()` — rules, auth/PIN/roles, billing/money — Sonnet evidence **and Dan’s approval** are required before merge regardless of confidence). When `confidence:` is **under 97%**, Spot must ask Dan before merge. Deploy authorization unchanged (Dan approves every deploy).

**Sonnet policy (Dan 2026-10-11):** Sonnet stays **required, no end date**, on the same paths as `requiresSonnetBackup()` in `gate-check.mjs`: `firestore.rules`; `src/` or `functions/` paths matching auth/PIN/roles heuristic; billing/money in product paths; plus ladder step 5, Grok FAIL/HIGH finding, or Dan asks. When the gate requires Sonnet, **run it without asking** — no optional Sonnet runs. Every Sonnet run records that run's `job-type:` and `sonnet-unique-findings:` (what Sonnet caught that Grok missed). CI/gate-config-only HIGH does **not** require Sonnet. Vendor-session-gated callables do **not** trigger Sonnet unless the **path** matches that heuristic (do not expand or shrink the heuristic).

**MODEL EVIDENCE tally (Dan only):** After **10 clean jobs of the same `job-type`** (Sonnet ran and caught nothing Grok missed; any Sonnet-only catch resets that type’s count to 0), the tally may **SUGGEST** dropping Sonnet for that type. **Dan decides. Nothing in the harness drops Sonnet automatically.** No counters or auto-switch in CI.

## Risk tiers (classify by path before you edit)

Use `npm run gate:tier` — implementation in `scripts/gate-check.mjs` (`classifyDiffTier` / `classifyPath`).

**HIGH** — `firestore.rules`; auth / PIN / roles (client or CF path heuristic); **all Cloud Functions under `functions/` except `functions/lib/`** (D-28); billing/money in `src/` or `functions/`; CI / gate config (`.github/workflows/`, `firebase.json`, `scripts/gate-check.mjs`, `scripts/install-git-hooks.mjs`, `scripts/ship-evidence-preflight.mjs`, root `package.json` scripts / deploy wiring / firebase major). Ambiguous → HIGH.

**MEDIUM** — two or more substantive product paths, or other non-excluded changes that are not LOW.

**LOW** — docs, `PROJECT_STATUS/`, `.cursor/`, `AGENTS.md`, `README`, or a **single** non-auth `src/` UI change with no other substantive paths.

## Coding ladder (Composer first)

Record the highest step reached in the PR body as `ladder-step: 1` … `ladder-step: 5`.

1. Composer writes the code and runs its own checks (build, tests, self-check).
2. If those checks fail **once**, escalate to Grok, who iterates with Composer.
3. If Composer still fails, Grok gives **exact, specific** instructions and Composer gets **one** more attempt.
4. If that fails, Grok writes the code for **that issue** itself and verifies it.
5. Grok escalates to Sonnet **only** after Grok has tried and determined it cannot solve the problem.

## Reviews

- Composer 2.5 Fast does all routine coding (UI and non-UI).
- **Parent/orchestrator** checks **scope and stray files only** (planned paths vs diff). The **separate** HIGH/accuracy reviewer does the deep read.
- Reviewers **cite CI results** instead of re-running full suites unless CI is unavailable. The independent reviewer still reads the **full diff**. CI must still pass; gate-check unchanged.
- **Grok always reviews all Composer-written code** for accuracy before a PR is marked ready — **every tier, including LOW**.
- **HIGH:** Grok review may **double** as the required security review if it covers security. Record `security-gate-id:` (lowercase UUID or `bc-<uuid>`) **and** `model: <exact gate slug>` (`model-self-report:` is separate and does not count). Required reviewer: **Grok 4.7, reasoning_effort HIGH, fast OFF, context 256k** — dispatch / `model:` slug **`grok-4.7-high`**. Grandfathered `cursor-grok-4.6-high` only on GitHub PR **#258** or **#259** (mechanical `GATE_PR_NUMBER`). Reject `NOT RUN`, empty, and junk. `-fast`, `xhigh`, 500k/max context, and non-allowlist Grok slugs never count. This **replaces** `sonnet-instruct`, `high-risk-adversarial`, and `sonnet-verify`. If the accuracy review did not cover security, run a separate Grok security review and record the same lines.
- **Sonnet on rules/auth/billing/money:** record **both** Grok allowlisted `model:` and `claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` when `requiresSonnetBackup()` applies — **required, no end date** (gate-check enforced). Also Sonnet when Grok returns FAIL/HIGH, ladder step 5, or Dan asks.
- **MEDIUM / LOW:** Grok accuracy review. No `security-gate-id` unless the change is HIGH.
- **Dropped:** `solution-verifier`, `build-checker`, `ship-verifier`. Do not run them.
- **UI screenshots:** only for **big** visual changes (theme, contrast, complex layout, redesign). Not for copy, labels, or small CSS.

### Reviewed commit (HIGH — gate-check enforced)

Order: **commit → HIGH review of that exact SHA → open the draft PR** with the review-evidence block already present, including `reviewed-commit: <sha>`. Do **not** open the PR first (avoids false-red).

After HIGH review, **later commits require re-review** unless they are **test-fixture only** (`**/fixtures/**`, `**/testdata/**`, `**/__fixtures__/**`, or `*fixture*` in the filename). `*.test.mjs` and test-logic changes are **not** fixture-only. Fixture-only follow-ups must be listed in the PR body as `post-review-commits: <sha> …` and CI must stay green. Merge still requires green PR CI.

HIGH review how-to (on-demand): `.cursor/rules/security-review-gate.mdc`. Cloud agents may record `security-gate-id: bc-<uuid>` from a real security-review run — do not invent ids.

### Open PRs before a gate or process merge

Merge or close open PRs before a gate or process change merges, or batch that change into those PRs, so open PRs are not forced into a re-review. As of 2026-10-11, GitHub PRs **#258** and **#259** are open.

### CI watch

The builder stops after handing off the PR. Builders never subscribe to CI on their own PR. Only the orchestrator, or Spot, watches CI.

## Tests are the safety net

CI on every PR must pass: `npm ci`, app build, functions build (committed `functions/lib` must match fresh build), `tsc`, and the Firestore emulator suites in `.github/workflows/pr-ci.yml`. Do not merge on red CI.

## Non-negotiables

1. A **real recorded** HIGH review (`security-gate-id:` + `model:` + `reviewed-commit:` when HIGH).
2. Tests and the build pass before merge.
3. **Merge:** No auto-merge except **D-95** Spot path (≥97% `confidence:`, Grok accuracy **PASS**, green CI, HIGH evidence when HIGH, `sonnet-ran:` **no**). Under 97% confidence, Spot asks Dan first. Sonnet-backup paths and `sonnet-ran:` **required** still need Sonnet + **Dan** before merge regardless of confidence. **Deploy:** Dan authorizes every deploy. No auto-deploy. Draft PRs are the default from cloud.
4. A **rollback point** (commit hash / prior CF revision) before every deploy, and a **smoke test** after.
5. **No gate bypass.** Do not use `GATE_SKIP`, `--no-verify`, or forged ids to skip HIGH review. Local `GATE_SKIP` / `--no-verify` only affect the optional pre-push hook — **CI `gate-check` always runs** and never honors `GATE_SKIP`.
6. One small job / one small PR per agent; MODEL EVIDENCE + notes in the PR body including `ladder-step:`, `confidence:`, and `context-used:`.
7. **256k context cap** — standard context only; stop and hand off before approaching the limit.

## Merge and deploy

Branch + PR. **Merge (D-95):** Spot may merge without asking Dan only when `confidence:` ≥97, Grok accuracy **PASS**, PR CI green, HIGH evidence when HIGH, and `sonnet-ran:` **no**; under 97%, ask Dan first; Sonnet-backup / `sonnet-ran:` **required** → Sonnet + Dan regardless of confidence. Dan authorizes deploy (gh-pages, Cloud Functions, Firestore rules) separately. After deploy: smoke the path you changed; keep the rollback hash ready.

## Minew / NDA

Never commit or paste Minew API docs, credentials, or platform internals. HTTP calls server-side only (`functions/src/`). Public UI uses StageVerify QR URLs (`#/r?`, `#/p?`) only.
